      ":question/problem": "![](images/3a/3a4526a6979a86aa924bddca54b05778e91bb67a1dcb6159c5436cc975b22668.png)\n\nA cyclist records the total distance traveled after $x$ minutes. The total distance traveled after $x$ minutes, in miles, is given by the function $D(x).$ The graph of $D(x)$ is shown above.  \n\nApproximate the rate of change when $x=45$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=15.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=30$ and $x=45.$*\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $x=45$ is\n{{field-1}} miles per minute."
